{%- comment -%}
  One H1 per page.
  For: homepages where the logo, collection tiles or featured products are all
  wrapped in <h1>, which gives search engines and screen readers no clear page title.

  1) Logo in the header section. Only the homepage gets an H1 from the logo;
     every other page gets its H1 from the page, product or collection title.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if request.page_type == 'index' -%}
  <h1 class="site-header__logo" style="margin:0">
{%- else -%}
  <div class="site-header__logo">
{%- endif -%}
    <a href="{{ routes.root_url }}">
      {%- if logo -%}
        <img src="{{ logo | image_url: width: 500 }}" width="{{ logo.width }}" height="{{ logo.height }}" alt="{{ logo.alt | default: shop.name | escape }}">
      {%- else -%}
        {{ shop.name }}
      {%- endif -%}
    </a>
{%- if request.page_type == 'index' -%}
  </h1>
{%- else -%}
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%}
  2) In each homepage section file (collection list, featured product, image with
     text), change the section heading tag from h1 to h2 and keep its class so the
     styling does not change:

       before:  <h1 class="h3">{{ collection.title }}</h1>
       after:   <h2 class="h3">{{ collection.title }}</h2>

     Search the theme code for "<h1" and you should end with exactly one per template.
{%- endcomment -%}
